WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.260
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Thursday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.150
We get a say. America voted,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.600
and data centres lost nearly all of about 40 local votes.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.680
Texas and Georgia also elected governors

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.470
who campaigned to pause new data centres.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.400
Over in China, Tencent's newest AI model can now see, and use a computer too.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.060
Tencent says it already tuned the training setup for its smaller siblings.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.200
AI, improving AI.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.140
Anthropic showed how to prove which AI wrote an answer.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.770
Think of it as a signature.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.780
And OpenAI's buying Pierre, a developer tools start-up.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.070
Axios calls it a shot at GitHub.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.430
Now, the money. AMD's revenue jumped 45%,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.200
and its data centre business nearly doubled.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.030
Data centre stocks slid. Elon Musk posted,

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.630
"Data centers in space looking pretty appealing right now."

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.550
Meanwhile, Chinese tech giants have reportedly ordered 6 million Nvidia chips.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.320
About $70 billion worth.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.500
Their own guess? They'll get about 1% of them in the next four months.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.770
In Singapore,

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.660
a new app built with Google DeepMind warns you about scam messages as they arrive.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.840
And Apple's AI finally reached China,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.010
in a test version, with help from Alibaba's Qwen.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.960
The catch? A Brazilian court told Meta to stop training on local news.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.430
And Uber says AI agents booked just four rides last quarter. Four.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.070
Now, the machines.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:08.500
Xiaomi showed two humanoid robots working a full 8-hour shift in its car factory.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.380
In Shanghai, six robots ran a convenience store for a full day,

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.970
making 147 coffees.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.660
Only four passed probation. The cleaner found a full bin and wandered outside.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.350
So yes, the machines keep clocking in. But we still get a say in how.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
